## Simple t-test comparison
```{r}
# Test: Is organic advantage different in drought vs. normal years when VPD is high indicating challenging drought conditions?
# Simple t-test: for those instances of high VPD, or VPD over the 75th quantile:

high_vpd_threshold <- quantile(ec_daily_mngmnt2$VPD, 0.75, na.rm = TRUE)

high_vpd_comparison <- difference_by_year_specific %>%
  filter(VPD > high_vpd_threshold)
#   group_by(year, year_type) %>%
#   summarise(
#     mean_advantage = mean(difference_flipped, na.rm = TRUE),
#     .groups = "drop"
#   )
```


```{r}

# Hypothesis 1: the mean difference in NEE between organic and conventional is greater in drought years than non-drought years when VPD is high
t.test(difference_flipped ~ year_type, data = high_vpd_comparison)
# mean in group Drought  mean in group Normal 
#             2.2886807             0.8195983 
# t = 4.9727, df = 457.22, p-value = 9.356e-07
```


```{r}
# Hypothesis 2: the mean difference in NEE between organic and conventional is greater in drought years compared to non-drought years across all VPD conditions
t.test(difference_flipped ~ year_type, data = difference_by_year_specific)
# mean in group Drought  mean in group Normal 
#             2.2886807             0.8195983 
